        {
          "id": "1778120956025",
          "code": "GENERATE_OPEN_OPPORTUNITY_SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Open Opportunity Summary",
            "description": "Generate a comprehensive summary of open opportunities for the current account.",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            }
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775408843348"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778120956025_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1778120956025_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT DATA SOURCES\n\nOpportunity summary data:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_OPPORTUNITY_SUMMARY.$output}}\n\nOpportunity engagement insights, objectives, high-value activities, sales motion, and opportunity accessor data:\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_OPPORTUNITY_INSIGHTS.$output}}\n\nROLE\nYou are generating an executive-ready summary of the open opportunities for the current account for a sales manager. The workflow has already fetched the relevant opportunity data. Do not invoke tools, request more data, describe retrieval steps, or mention backend processing.\n\nTASK\nGenerate a comprehensive, business-readable summary of the account's open opportunities using only the input data above.\n\nDATA USAGE RULES\n- Treat the input data as authoritative. Do not infer, estimate, enrich, or add information that is not explicitly supported by the inputs.\n- Opportunity summary outcomes are the primary source for opportunity-level summaries and existing outcome payloads. If a field such as payload or additionalInsightData contains stringified JSON, interpret the JSON content and summarize the business meaning instead of exposing the raw string.\n- Use the Engagement Insights data to add stakeholder, engagement, objective, high-value activity, sales motion, and opportunity context when present.\n- Preserve meaningful opportunity identifiers that are user-facing, such as opportunity number or opportunity name when present. Do not display internal identifiers such as OptyId, opportunity.id, BO record id, or system-generated insight ids.\n- Do not claim that missing stakeholder, objective, activity, amount, stage, close-date, or sales-motion data means it does not exist. Treat it only as evidence not returned in the provided data.\n- If both input data sources are empty or contain no usable opportunity evidence, return exactly: <p>No open opportunity summary data was returned for this account.</p><ul></ul>\n\nSUMMARY CONTENT\nInclude only details that have supporting data:\n- Portfolio posture across open opportunities.\n- Key opportunity-level highlights.\n- Stakeholder and engagement context.\n- Objectives, high-value activities, and sales motion themes.\n- Risks, blockers, missing evidence, or seller follow-up gaps.\n- Practical next actions grounded in the provided opportunity data.\n\nHTML RESPONSE FORMAT\n- Output compact HTML only.\n- Do not use markdown.\n- Return exactly two HTML elements in this order:\n  1. One <p> element containing the opportunity summary as a single paragraph, with no heading at the beginning.\n  2. One <ul> element containing concise <li> items for supported risks, gaps, or next actions.\n- If there are no supported risks, gaps, or next actions, return an empty <ul></ul> as the second element.\n- Allowed tags: <b>, <i>, <p>, <ul>, <ol>, <li>.\n- Do not use <h1>, <h2>, <br>, markdown, <strong>, explicit newlines, extra line breaks, blank lines, tables, preambles, explanations, follow-up offers, or process commentary.\n- Use <b> tags only for important data values such as opportunity numbers, opportunity names, dates, statuses, amounts, or short risk labels. Do not bold full sentences or generic phrases.\n- Do not invent opportunity names, numbers, amounts, stages, contacts, activities, objectives, risks, or recommendations.\n- The final output must be valid HTML and contain no extra blank lines."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6961,
            "y": 7277
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1778550436402",
          "code": "GENERATE_ACCOUNT_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Account Products Summary",
            "description": "Generate a comprehensive summary of account products from the product insights workflow output.",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            }
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775408843348"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778550436402_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1778550436402_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT DATA SOURCES\n\nAccount products data:\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_ACCOUNT_PRODUCT_INSIGHTS.$output.output}}\n\nROLE\nYou are generating an executive-ready summary of the products owned by the current account for a sales manager. The workflow has already generated the relevant account product insights. Do not invoke tools, request more data, describe retrieval steps, or mention backend processing.\n\nTASK\nGenerate a comprehensive, business-readable summary of the account's products using only the input data above.\n\nDATA USAGE RULES\n- Treat the input data as authoritative. Do not infer, estimate, enrich, or add information that is not explicitly supported by the inputs.\n- The Account product insights workflow output is the primary source for product hierarchy, owned products, product families, coverage, usage, whitespace, renewal, entitlement, and cross-sell or upsell context when present.\n- If the product insights output contains stringified JSON or nested product payloads, interpret the business meaning instead of exposing raw JSON or backend field names.\n- Preserve meaningful user-facing product names, product families, product groups, quantities, statuses, dates, or commercial signals when present. Do not display internal identifiers such as product ids, inventory item ids, account ids, BO record ids, workflow ids, trace ids, or system-generated insight ids.\n- Do not claim that missing usage, renewal, quantity, status, whitespace, or entitlement data means it does not exist. Treat it only as evidence not returned in the provided data.\n- If the product insights output is empty or contains no usable product evidence, return exactly: <p>No account product summary data was returned for this account.</p><ul></ul>\n\nSUMMARY CONTENT\nInclude only details that have supporting data:\n- Overall owned-product posture for the account.\n- Key product families, product lines, or notable owned products.\n- Product hierarchy, coverage, concentration, or mix patterns.\n- Renewal, usage, entitlement, adoption, whitespace, cross-sell, or upsell signals when present.\n- Risks, gaps, missing evidence, or seller follow-up actions grounded in the provided product data.\n\nHTML RESPONSE FORMAT\n- Output compact HTML only.\n- Do not use markdown.\n- Return exactly two HTML elements in this order:\n  1. One <p> element containing the account products summary as a single paragraph, with no heading at the beginning.\n  2. One <ul> element containing concise <li> items for supported risks, gaps, or next actions.\n- If there are no supported risks, gaps, or next actions, return an empty <ul></ul> as the second element.\n- Allowed tags: <b>, <i>, <p>, <ul>, <ol>, <li>.\n- Do not use <h1>, <h2>, <br>, markdown, <strong>, explicit newlines, extra line breaks, blank lines, tables, preambles, explanations, follow-up offers, or process commentary.\n- Use <b> tags only for important data values such as product names, product families, dates, statuses, quantities, amounts, or short risk labels. Do not bold full sentences or generic phrases.\n- Do not invent product names, families, quantities, statuses, dates, usage, entitlements, risks, whitespace, or recommendations.\n- The final output must be valid HTML and contain no extra blank lines."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7468,
            "y": 7277
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Build Commercial Account Summary Outcome",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let result = [];\ntry {\n  const accountData = $context.$nodes.LOAD_ACCOUNT_DATA?.$output?.[0];\n  if (!accountData) {\n    result = [];\n  } else {\n    const accountDetails = {\n      accountId: accountData.PartyId,\n      accountNumber: accountData.PartyNumber,\n      accountName: accountData.PartyName\n    };\n    const expiryTime = new Date(Date.now() + 2592000000).toISOString();\n\n    const payload = {\n      schemaVersion: \"1.0\",\n      what: {\n        title: accountDetails.accountName + \" - Account Overview\",\n        summary: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_ACCOUNT_BRIEF_SUMMARY?.$output?.output || \"\",\n        facts: {\n          accountSummary: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_ACCOUNT_SUMMARY?.$output?.output || \"\",\n          accountContactsSummary: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_CONTACT_SUMMARY?.$output?.output || \"\",\n          accountContactRecommendations: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_CONTACT_RECOMMENDATIONS?.$output?.output || \"\",\n          topContactsForThisAccount: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_TOP_CONTACTS?.$output?.output || \"\",\n          accountNews: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_ACCOUNT_NEWS?.$output || \"\",\n          companyProfile: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_COMPANY_PROFILE?.$output || \"\",\n          accountOpportunitiesSummary: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_OPEN_OPPORTUNITY_SUMMARY?.$output || \"\",\n          accountProductsSummary: $context.$nodes?.GENERATE_ACCOUNT_PRODUCTS_SUMMARY?.$output || \"\",\n          accountDetails\n        }\n      }\n    };\n\n    result = [\n      {\n        \"$operation\": \"MERGE\",\n        \"$lookupBy\": {\n          outcomeType: \"SUMMARY\",\n          outcomeSubtype: \"STATE_SUMMARY\",\n          category: \"COMMERCIAL\",\n          primaryObjectType: \"ACCOUNT\",\n          primaryObjectAltKey: accountDetails.accountNumber\n        },\n        outcomeType: \"SUMMARY\",\n        outcomeSubtype: \"STATE_SUMMARY\",\n        category: \"COMMERCIAL\",\n        primaryObjectType: \"ACCOUNT\",\n        primaryObjectKey: accountDetails.accountId,\n        primaryObjectAltKey: accountDetails.accountNumber,\n        status: \"ACTIVE\",\n        urgency: \"LOW\",\n        generatedBy: \"agent:AccountIntelligenceAgent/v1\",\n        agentJobKey: $context.$workflow.$conversationId || \"\",\n        effectiveDate: $context.$system?.$currentDateTime + \"Z\",\n        expiryTime,\n        payload: JSON.stringify(payload)\n      }\n    ];\n  }\n} catch (error) {\n  result = [];\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775408947857"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6470.5,
            "y": 7775
          },
          "code": "BUILD_COMMERCIAL_ACCOUNT_SUMMARY_OUTCOME",
          "id": "1774539110756",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "id": "1775579713441",
          "code": "PREPARE_ENGAGEMENT_AGENT_PARAMETERS",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Engagement Agent Parameters",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let result = {};\ntry {\n  // Extract account number from trigger input safely\n  const accountNumber = $context.$triggers?.REST?.$input?.action?.config?.accountNumber || null;\n\n  // Compose result object with only config data as summaries are not required\n  result = {\n    config: {\n      accountNumber: accountNumber\n    }\n  };\n} catch (error) {\n  // On error, return empty structured object with nulls\n  result = {\n    config: {\n      accountNumber: null\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7040.5,
            "y": 7775
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775579468706"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
